From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:17:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: gemini-lid: hold the backlight off apart from the
 display's state

0755 lights the backlight on open only if it was lit at the close. A
display that blanks while the lid is closed is missed: on the Gemini,
with a charger attached the lid close does not suspend, the desktop's
idle timeout turned the display off while the lid was closed, and the
open lit the backlight behind the dark panel until a key press woke the
display.

The policy and the panel used the same state, the backlight's power and
blank flags, so the policy could not tell what the display wanted. Hold
the backlight off with BL_CORE_SUSPENDED instead, which nothing else
sets on this board, and leave the power and blank state to the panel
and DPMS. The backlight is lit only while neither holds it off: on open
it lights again only if the display is still on, and a later unblank
lights it as usual. A display that unblanks while the lid is closed
stays dark until the open.
---
 drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c | 21 ++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c b/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
index 00fbf68b2..89a2b4154 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
@@ -25,8 +25,6 @@ static DEFINE_MUTEX(lid_lock);
 static struct input_dev *lid_keyboard;
 static bool lid_exiting;
 static bool lid_applied_closed;
-/* The backlight was lit when the lid closed, so the open lights it again. */
-static bool lid_backlight_was_on;
 
 static void gemini_lid_apply(bool closed)
 {
@@ -50,16 +48,17 @@ static void gemini_lid_apply(bool closed)
 		mutex_lock(&bd->ops_lock);
 		if (bd->ops) {
 			/*
-			 * Restore only what the close turned off: a display
-			 * blanked before the close, by DPMS or a console blank,
-			 * stays dark, with no backlight behind a sleeping panel.
+			 * Hold the backlight off with its own flag, apart from
+			 * the power and blank state that the panel and DPMS
+			 * keep. On open it lights again only if the display
+			 * still wants it, however that changed while the lid
+			 * was closed, and a later unblank lights it as usual.
 			 */
-			if (closed) {
-				lid_backlight_was_on = !backlight_is_blank(bd);
-				backlight_disable(bd);
-			} else if (lid_backlight_was_on) {
-				backlight_enable(bd);
-			}
+			if (closed)
+				bd->props.state |= BL_CORE_SUSPENDED;
+			else
+				bd->props.state &= ~BL_CORE_SUSPENDED;
+			backlight_update_status(bd);
 		}
 		mutex_unlock(&bd->ops_lock);
 	}
